{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise validated on base ae6f2ac57a: ruff C901 census over src/rebar/graph reproduced the ticket's four hotspots EXACTLY — _find_direct_blockers 18, _get_all_blocked_by 20, check_cycle_at_level 16, detect_newly_unblocked 22. No sibling landing had moved or already-reduced them, so the plan stood as written.\n\nPlan-review: the inherited PASS attestation was foreign_key (signed by principal ade0f2ef, this env is b8a354e0), so review-plan was re-run here. First pass BLOCKed on G1G2: the plan named 'tests/unit + tests/interfaces' as the behavioral oracle, but neither contains any of these symbols — the real oracle is tests/scripts/graph/ plus tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py. Corrected that, and also applied the two apply-now advisories: (G6) specified the bfs contract as an ACCUMULATOR-returning walk rather than a visited-returning one, because _get_all_blocked_by returns 'blocked' — which excludes the seed and includes targets with no backing dir — so a visited-returning bfs would have silently changed check_would_create_cycle's membership test; (E6) added a characterization test for exactly that property, since no existing test pinned it. Second pass PASS + signed, only a deferred P6 (compound ACs). Claimed cleanly.\n\nImplementation landed as planned, behavior-preserving:\n- _loader.load_indexed_states — the reduce_all -> drop error/fsck -> index loop, previously duplicated verbatim in _find_direct_blockers and _compute_dep_graph, now defined once (reached via the reducer module attribute so the existing patch point still works).\n- _relations.bfs(starts, neighbors_fn) — accumulator BFS skeleton; visited is passed to neighbors_fn read-only because both callers consult it when deciding what to yield.\n- _blockers: split into _own_depends_on_blockers / _blocks_targeting (the two sources its own docstring already named), dedup preserved across the two.\n- _graph: _reduce_or_none / _blocks_targets / _dependents_of / _is_at_level / _same_level_neighbors extracted; check_cycle_at_level's mid-loop early return became 'source_id in bfs(...)' (equivalent: the seed cannot be source_id since the self-loop case returns first).\n- _unblock: _read_tombstone_status / _load_states_with_tombstones / _is_closed_after_batch / _was_already_unblocked / _select_newly_unblocked. Kept separate from load_indexed_states — tombstone semantics differ.\n- _ready.py, _status.py::_get_ticket_status and _unblock.py::batch_close_operations untouched, as scoped.\n\nResult: all four functions now measure CCN <= 7 (targets were <=8/<=8/<=8/<=12), so --update-stale REMOVED all four baseline entries rather than lowering them — they no longer exceed the 15 threshold at all. check_complexity_baseline.py --check: active=55 new=0 increased=0 stale=0.\n\nGates: 118/118 in tests/scripts/graph/ + tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py green with zero edits to existing tests; the new characterization test was verified passing on the PRE-refactor base first (it characterizes current behavior) and still passes after. make lint green, make typecheck green (518 files), all argument-less check_* gates exit 0, all four generators produce no diff. Full CI suite running now."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786599054466045001,"uuid":"6ccca89b-a88e-497c-b550-41976d2fb4b0"}